/-!
# Actual-node causal provenance for the concrete Tag-73 restoration client

This leaf strengthens the scheduler-native node-store induction.  The
restoration request rule is obtained by destructing the actual finite client;
it is not supplied per returned node.  Programming-ledger witnesses are
carried through the append-only store and are tied to literal earlier adjacent
fork pairs in the executable scheduler trace.

The final positive-transition field is composed only after the synchronized
native/dependent target-clean state alignment identifies cached and fresh
verifier replies at their actual request states.  No lookup-freshness,
acceptance, extraction, restore-function, or compiler conclusion is a field.
-/

